<title>MEXICO: Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Jan 18.</title>
<headline>Mexico 1996-1997 sugar harvest update to Jan 18.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's Agroindustry Sugar Committee weekly harvest update for the 1996-1997 (Nov/June) sugar crop to Jan 18 (sugar, in tonnes) --</p>
<p>Activity in week Jan 12-Jan 18</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     1,694,343 tns	183,561 tns    10.83 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     1,812,791 tns	188,314 tns    10.39 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     1,581,678 tns	165,470 tns    10.46 pct</p>
<p>Total activity to Jan 18</p>
<p>    Harvest	Cane milled	Sugar Output    Yield</p>
<p>     96-97     9,030,342 tns	899,597 tns     9.96 pct</p>
<p>     95-96     8,302,391 tns	792,770 tns     9.55 pct</p>
<p>     94-95     8,457,230 tns	821,342 tns     9.71 pct</p>
<p>The committee reported that during the week, 57 of the country's active 61 mills were in operation compared to 57 in the 1995-1996 harvest and 54 in the 1994-1995 harvest.</p>
<p>--Chris Aspin, Mexico City newsroom (525) 728 9530</p>
</text>
